<a name="2026-10-15-remembering-tj-porter"> </a>
<h3>Remembering TJ Porter</h3>
<p>Back in early 2015, I discovered an artist by the name of TJ Porter.
 He had just released an album called “A World Adrift”, and I downloaded
 this album on Bandcamp, and enjoyed listening to it a lot in those
 days, which were just a few short months after my first wife died.
<p>Later on TJ Porter made many more albums, and since the album was a
 “name your price” download, Bandcamp apparently had a quota about how
 much free music he could have on their servers, so this album got
 deleted to make room for his newer albums.
<p>A few years after that, TJ Porter <a href="https://tjporter.bandcamp.com/community">passed  away</a>.
<p>His newer music is still online at <a href="https://tjporter.bandcamp.com/">https:/<![if gt IE 6]>&#8203;<![endif]><wbr>/<![if gt IE 6]>&#8203;<![endif]><wbr>tjporter.bandcamp.com/<![if gt IE 6]>&#8203;<![endif]><wbr></a>.
<p>While “A World Adrift” is no longer on TJ Porter’s Bandcamp page, I
 downloaded it back then and am making available MP3s of his songs <a href="music/TjPorter-WorldAdrift-05.mp3">Gasterbeiter II</a> 
and <a href="music/TjPorter-WorldAdrift-06.mp3">Velvet Hammer</a> 
from that album so that these excellent songs are not
 lost in the sands of time.
<p>Some more information about this album is in a <a href="https://gearspace.com/threads/a-world-adrift-new-album.987768/">Gearspace  thread</a> 
announcing the album, as well as a <a href="https://www.progarchives.com/album.asp?id=52067">third party description of the album</a>.
<p>TJ Porter used the following synths to make this now-lost album: Moog
 Minitaur, Arturia Minibrute, Korg R3, Korg EMX, Korg Volca Bass,
 Waldorf Pulse 2, Waldorf Streichfett, Waldorf Rocket, Novation
 BassStation Rack, Roland JV-1080
<a name="2026-10-15-solution-to-mating-puzzle"> </a>
<h3>Solution to mating puzzle</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>1. Qb5+ [any legal move] 2. Qb8+ Kd7 (or Bc8) 3. Qc8#
</li>
</ul>


